    2. Decide marker assignment -- pick 1-2 lanes as red-marked (source), 1 lane as green-marked (destination), rest unmarked. Choose sprite counts per lane (1-3 each).
    3. Build the OUTPUT first -- green lane has its original sprites plus N new sprites (N = total red sprites) stacked upward at period 4. Verify total green lane sprites fit (top_row >= 1). Red lane sprites colored grey(5). Unmarked lanes unchanged.
    4. Derive INPUT from output -- replace grey sprites in red lanes with their original colors. Add N new sprites' positions in green lane back to bg. Place red(2) and green(3) marker bars at row 29 under marked lanes.
